# Project workflow

- Remote: only `preshan/ai-native-fullstack-challenge-laravel-nextjs` (my fork). Never touch upstream.
- Never push, open a PR, add collaborators, change visibility or deploy without an explicit request.
- Ask before every commit and every push. One concern per commit.
- Stage explicit paths only. Never `git add -A` or `git add .` at the repo root.
- Before committing, show `git status --short` and `git diff --cached --stat`, and flag anything
  staged that the message does not describe.
- Unknown commits, files or branches: stop and ask.
- Do not reformat or refactor starter files a task does not need.
- No em dashes, en dashes or arrow characters in docs, comments, commit messages or cards.
- Never claim a check that was not run. Quote the real command and its output.
- Do not code a task until its plan is approved.

## Commits

Conventional Commits, imperative, under 72 characters. Types: feat, fix, refactor, test, chore,
docs, perf, ci. Scopes: api, web, ci, db. Body says why and any behaviour change.

- Good: `fix(api): remove N+1 from request list`
- Bad: `Fixed stuff and updated tests` (no type, past tense, two concerns)

## Verify before done

```
docker compose exec api php artisan test
docker compose exec api vendor/bin/pint --test <changed files>
docker compose exec web npm run typecheck
```

## Notes and decisions

- Every deliberate behaviour change (status codes, limits, response shape) is recorded.
- Drafts live outside the repo in `/Users/preshan/Documents/Gapstars/baseline-evidence-2026-11-12/`
  (`AI_USAGE.md`, `DECISIONS.md`). Never edit the repo copies; the owner writes those by hand.
- Measure before and after on the same seed, and prove unchanged output with a checksum.
